{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://agent-cost-analyzer/views.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Answers \"what is driving my spend?\" across every available provider (or one, with `provider`) in a date window, optionally for one repository or project: token and AI Credits totals with coverage, per-basis cost totals, cache hit ratio, spend by provider, model, day, repository, project, vendor and channel, the most expensive sessions, and `reconciliation` (Copilot's billed AI Credits against the price book, per model and month: a steady gap means the price book is out of date). Follow up with get_session_cost on a top session. The same data the web Dashboard shows. `active`: true marks a session whose latest turn started in the last 15 minutes; its figures may still change. Cost figures carry their basis: billed (what GitHub Copilot billed, AI Credits), reported (what the agent logged itself, USD) and priced (tokens \u00d7 the price version in force on the turn's channel at the turn's time; see get_price_book, and priceVersionIds). The preferred figure is billed, else reported, else priced. A priced figure with apiEquivalent: true is what the same use costs on the API, though a flat-fee plan may have covered it. A priced figure with userPriceVersionIds used price versions the user added themselves (not bundled prices); say so when you quote it. An unknown figure is {known:false, reason}, never 0; totals give knownTurns of turns per basis. Currencies stay apart; `usd` converts only at 1 AI Credit = $0.01.","inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","properties":{"limit":{"description":"How many of the most recent sessions to read per provider (default 50, max 500).","exclusiveMinimum":0,"maximum":500,"type":"integer"},"projectId":{"description":"Only turns in this project (from list_projects).","